          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This is an Important denial of service vulnerability in Netty's HTTP content decompression. A remote attacker can exploit this flaw by sending specially crafted compressed payloads using Brotli, Zstandard, or Snappy encodings, bypassing configured decompression limits. This leads to unbounded memory allocation, potentially causing an out-of-memory condition and rendering affected Red Hat systems unavailable.",
            "title": "Statement"
