            "text": "This flaw is rated as Important as it allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to cause a denial of service in applications utilizing `netty-codec-redis` or `netty-handler`. By sending specially crafted Redis payloads without proper termination, an attacker can exhaust the server's direct memory pool, preventing legitimate connections and disrupting service availability. This impacts Red Hat products that process Redis traffic via affected Netty components.",
