            },
            "url": "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:37390"
          },
          {
            "category": "workaround",
            "details": "To mitigate this issue, configure applications utilizing Netty's `SslClientHelloHandler` to specify a non-zero value for the `maxClientHelloLength` parameter. This will enable the internal length validation, preventing the eager allocation of large memory buffers when processing crafted TLS ClientHello messages. Refer to your specific application's documentation for details on configuring Netty's TLS handler. A restart of the affected application or service is required for the configuration changes to take effect.",
            "product_ids": [
              "Red Hat build of Apache Camel 4.18.1.P1 for Spring Boot 3.5.16"
            ]
          }
