        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in containerd package. Containers launched with a User set as a UID:GID larger than the maximum 32-bit signed integer can cause an overflow condition where the container ultimately runs as root (UID 0). This issue could cause unexpected behavior for environments that require containers to run as a non-root user.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "containerd: containerd has an integer overflow in User ID handling",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "For Red Hat OpenShift GitOps and OpenShift Container Platform deployments, image sources are controlled through OpenShift's Image configuration and RBAC policies. Administrators can restrict image imports to trusted registries using allowedRegistriesForImport and registrySources configuration.In typical GitOps deployments, application images are pulled from pre-approved registries configured by platform administrators.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
